139
00:09:54,462 --> 00:09:54,744
Rym: It is.

140
00:09:54,805 --> 00:09:57,160
Rym: The Passion of the Christ was the previous winner.

141
00:09:58,621 --> 00:10:08,060
Rym: So we saw it, and to give you a little geek bite, what's interesting is that, like, it's Deadpool, so if you are a fan of Deadpool's schtick, it's that to the end.

142
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:12,080
Rym: Like, if you like Deadpool, this movie might be your Citizen Kane.

143
00:10:12,722 --> 00:10:15,140
Rym: Like, you're gonna get the maximum possible Deadpool.

144
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:19,160
Rym: If you don't like Deadpool's deal, you will not like this movie.

145
00:10:19,701 --> 00:10:23,460
Rym: This movie is not for you if you don't like Deadpool as a concept.

146
00:10:23,722 --> 00:10:25,680
Rym: Like, it's pretty hard there.

147
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:29,320
Rym: This is not like the Spider-Man movie that someone who hates comics will love.

148
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,240
Rym: Like, no, if you don't like Deadpool, you're not gonna like this movie.

149
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,692
Rym: But I really enjoyed it.

150
00:10:33,793 --> 00:10:58,400
Rym: It was a pretty good movie, and it was, if I wanted to put on my lit crit hat without getting into any details, I would say that this movie is addressing, whether or not this is intentional or not, the same fundamental thing that the Spider-Verse movies are dealing with, but in the opposite way and from the opposite side of that lit crit conversation.

151
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:08,880
Rym: Like, you wanna have that conversation from an art cinematic masterpiece standpoint of a highly refined creative vision drawn to perfect execution?

152
00:11:09,280 --> 00:11:09,778
Rym: Spider-Verse.

153
00:11:10,261 --> 00:11:25,540
Rym: If you wanna get that same message with a guy saying fuck a lot and gross stuff happening constantly and Deadpool doing Deadpool stuff, then yeah, you can watch Deadpool to get to many of the same conclusions and many of the same lit crit and philosophical ideas.

154
00:11:26,782 --> 00:11:29,599
Rym: So, I don't know, without getting too deep into it, I enjoyed it.

155
00:11:30,161 --> 00:11:36,799
Rym: Like, kinda glad I saw it in the theater, but like all MCU movies, it's not a movie I necessarily need to see more than once.

156
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:45,880
